# Python standards

- Use Python 3.11 and fully typed Pydantic models at every external boundary.
- Routers validate and delegate; domain services own behavior; repositories own SQL.
- Use explicit transactions, revision checks, idempotency keys, and typed errors.
- Never log credentials, verification codes, passwords, tokens, or raw model reasoning.
- Use timezone-aware UTC values and stable UUIDv7 text identifiers.
- Add unit, contract, integration, and adversarial tests beside every new behavior.

